  "causalConclusion": "Installed form CSRF/origin middleware rejects before credential verification; native error flows to application after-hook. The current helper labels every APIError non-success, and the hook treats every non-success as a wrong-password attempt without checking failure eligibility.",
  "sourceDerivedImplications": [
    "A supplied account can acquire failed-attempt bookkeeping on a rejected origin request before admitted credential verification. Actual probes supplied valid synthetic credentials.",
    "Repeated rejection can reach the existing failure threshold by source analysis; actual threshold crossing and expired-lock reset behavior were not exercised."
  ],
  "nextRepair": "Refresh/harden the narrow credential outcome eligibility and hook ordering, preserving genuine wrong-password and successful-login bookkeeping, unavailable-account semantics and current-session guards; rebuild and independently requalify changed source.",
